mode script

// The bang (`!`, which a subscript parses to) panics on an uncaught
// throw. Its message is compiler-synthesized, and it used to pass the
// source location as a message PART while panic also prints its own
// `loc` -- so the location appeared twice and ran straight into the type
// name: "...:6:10: panic: ...:6:10OutOfBounds". The location now goes in
// panic's `loc` argument, leaving one location and a readable sentence.
// Expected exit code is 1 (panic exits non-zero).

mut v := Vec(I64).new()
v.push(own 7)
println(v[0].to_str())
println(v[9].to_str())
